    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. Could you go into a bit more detail on the maintenance for each? Especially if we're worried about the floor looking \"beat up\" after a year or two of people walking through with hard-soled shoes or dragging things across it. I want to know which one stays looking the newest for the longest.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Polished concrete typically requires occasional sealing to maintain its high shine, and while durable, heavy abrasion can subtly dull the finish over time. LVT is extremely low-maintenance; routine sweeping and occasional spot cleaning usually suffice to keep it looking pristine. Natural stone will likely require periodic professional cleaning and sealing to prevent dulling or staining from scuffs and dirt, which can make it appear aged faster than the other options.",
      "source": "target",
